content.text:
Based on my thorough exploration of the pantoken monorepo, here's a detailed structured report on how themes and color schemes are emitted, applied, and potential collision points when two independent pantoken instances live on the same page.

## 1. CSS Emission: Theme/Scheme Variants & Selectors

### Token Sheet Structure  
[formats/css/src/emit.ts](formats/css/src/emit.ts#L1-L80) generates CSS with:
- **`@property` registrations** (global, `:root`-scoped): Concrete tokens with `syntax` + `initial-value`
  ```ts
  @property --instui-color-brand {
    syntax: "<color>";
    inherits: true;
    initial-value: #0374b5;
  }
  ```
- **Scoped declarations**: Contextual tokens (`var()`, `light-dark()`) under a selector (default `:root`)

### Theme Variant Emission

**Default theme (rebrand)** — [formats/css/src/index.ts](formats/css/src/index.ts#L25-L45):
```ts
export const css: string = themedCss("rebrand");  // Full @property registrations + :root declarations
```

**Multi-theme site** — [docs/scripts/site-themes.ts](docs/scripts/site-themes.ts#L1-L80):
- Emits `rebrand` in full (all `@property` + `:root` defaults)
- Other themes (canvas, canvasHighContrast) as `:root[data-pantoken-theme="…"]` with only **differing** tokens
```ts
:root[data-pantoken-theme="canvas"] {
  --instui-color-brand: var(--instui-primitive-color-canvas-canvas70);
  /* only tokens whose value differs from rebrand default */
}
```

### Light/Dark Handling

**`light-dark()` function**: Emitted in token values for `rebrand` only (single-mode themes like `canvas` flatten to light-only)  
[formats/css/src/theme-variants.ts](formats/css/src/theme-variants.ts#L25-L40):
```ts
const lightBranch = (value: string): string | null => {
  // Extract the light branch from `light-dark(light-val, dark-val)`
};
```

**VitePress uses CSS fallback**: [docs/.vitepress/theme/pantoken.css](docs/.vitepress/theme/pantoken.css#L30-L50)
```css
:root {
  color-scheme: light;  /* Vite's prod transform lowers light-dark() using this */
}
@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
  :root {
    color-scheme: dark;
  }
}
```

### Scope Mechanism

**Default scope: `:root`** — [formats/css/src/to-css.ts](formats/css/src/to-css.ts#L60-L90)  
Customizable via `ToCssOptions.scope`:
```ts
export function toCss(tokens: readonly Token[], options: ToCssOptions = {}): string {
  const { scope = ":root", plugins = [] } = options;
  // All declarations wrapped in `${scope} { … }`
}
```

**Pendo renderer**: Scopes to guide container — [renderers/pendo/src/build.ts](renderers/pendo/src/build.ts#L29-L50)
```ts
@scope ([class*="instui"]._pendo-step-container) {
  @layer pantoken { --instui-color-brand: var(--instui-primitive-color-navy-navy70); }
}
```

### Custom Theme Colors

**Two variants exist**:  
1. [plugins/pantoken/custom-theme-colors/src/index.ts](plugins/pantoken/custom-theme-colors/src/index.ts#L1-L20) emits `:root[data-pantoken-color="…"]` rules
2. `custom-theme-colors.scoped.css` (from [plugins/pantoken/custom-theme-colors/README.md](plugins/pantoken/custom-theme-colors/README.md#L16-L22)):
   - Matches `[data-pantoken-color]` on **any element**, not just `:root`
   - Canvas Theme Editor uses this for editable content wrappers

---

## 2. Runtime Theme Switching

### localStorage + Attribute Binding

**Docs site** — [docs/.vitepress/theme/theme.ts](docs/.vitepress/theme/theme.ts#L110-L130):
```ts
const STORAGE_KEY = "pantoken-theme";
const STORAGE_COLOR_KEY = "pantoken-color";

export function getStoredTheme(): PantokenTheme {
  if (typeof localStorage === "undefined") return "rebrand";
  const value = localStorage.getItem(STORAGE_KEY);
  return THEMES.some((t) => t.key === value) ? (value as PantokenTheme) : "rebrand";
}

export function applyTheme(theme: PantokenTheme): void {
  const html = document.documentElement;
  html.dataset.pantokenTheme = theme;  // ← Sets `<html data-pantoken-theme="rebrand">`
  persistTheme(theme);  // localStorage
  broadcastTheme(theme, getStoredColor());  // postMessage to iframes
}

export function applyColor(color: PantokenColor): void {
  const html = document.documentElement;
  html.dataset.pantokenColor = color;  // ← Sets `<html data-pantoken-color="navy">`
  persistColor(color);  // localStorage
  broadcastColor(color);  // postMessage to iframes
}
```

**Key collision point**: Both instances **share a single document.documentElement** and the same **localStorage namespace**. If both write to the same keys, they overwrite each other.

### postMessage Broadcasting

[docs/.vitepress/theme/theme.ts](docs/.vitepress/theme/theme.ts#L150-L180):
```ts
export function broadcastTheme(theme: PantokenTheme, color: PantokenColor): void {
  for (const frame of document.querySelectorAll<HTMLIFrameElement>(
    ".pantoken-demo__frame, .canvas-rce-page__frame"
  )) {
    frame.contentWindow?.postMessage(
      { type: "pantoken-demo-theme", theme, color, mode: getActiveScheme() },
      themeTargetOrigin(frame)
    );
  }
}

function themeTargetOrigin(frame: HTMLIFrameElement): string {
  if (!frame.hasAttribute("src")) return "*";  // srcdoc frames (opaque origin)
  try {
    return new URL(frame.src, window.location.href).origin;
  } catch {
    return window.location.origin;
  }
}
```

**Collision point**: Queries **all** `.pantoken-demo__frame` and `.canvas-rce-page__frame` on the page and broadcasts to them. If two pantoken instances both query the same DOM, they both send postMessages to **the same iframes**, potentially racing or conflicting.

---

## 3. Canvas Theme Editor Platform & Preview Iframe

### Theme Generation

[platforms/canvas-theme-editor/src/build-theme.ts](platforms/canvas-theme-editor/src/build-theme.ts#L50-L80):
- Generates uploadable `theme.css` and `theme.js` for Canvas LMS
- Includes `@pantoken/css` (lean sheets), `@pantoken/components` (base/components/utilities), and **element-scoped** `custom-theme-colors.scoped.css`
```ts
export function defaultThemeCssAssets(theme: ThemeVariant, mode: ThemeMode): CdnFile[] {
  return [
    tokenSheetFile(theme, mode),
    { package: "@pantoken/components", path: "dist/base.css" },
    { package: "@pantoken/components", path: "dist/components.css" },
    { package: "@pantoken/components", path: "dist/utilities.css" },
    {
      package: "@pantoken/plugin-custom-theme-colors",
      path: "dist/custom-theme-colors.scoped.css",  // ← Matches [data-pantoken-color] anywhere
    },
  ];
}
```

### Preview Frame Mechanism

**Scaffold template** — [packages/scaffold/templates/canvas-theme-editor/src/main.ts.tmpl](packages/scaffold/templates/canvas-theme-editor/src/main.ts.tmpl#L140-L150):
```ts
document.head.append(chromeThemeStyle);
// Canvas RCE embedded preview: receive theme via window.top postMessage or attribute
```

**No explicit iframe creation**: The platform generates CSS for Canvas's theme editor; preview logic is Canvas-side. Pantoken CSS ships as `theme.css` loaded into Canvas's document.

---

## 4. Docs Site Theme & Demo Embedding

### Site-Wide Theme Sheet

[docs/scripts/site-themes.ts](docs/scripts/site-themes.ts#L1-L80):
- Generates `.vitepress/theme/generated/site-themes.css` (pre-build step)
- Loaded by [docs/.vitepress/theme/index.ts](docs/.vitepress/theme/index.ts)
- Scopes each theme override to `:root[data-pantoken-theme="…"]`
- Includes `foundationPlugin` for elevation/focus-outline composites

### Demo Frame Broadcasting

**srcdoc iframes** — [tools/demo/src/srcdoc.ts](tools/demo/src/srcdoc.ts#L30-L50):
```js
// Boot script inside the iframe (minified):
var p=window.parent;
addEventListener("message",function(e){
  if(e.data.type==="pantoken-demo-theme"){
    if(e.data.theme){document.documentElement.dataset.pantokenTheme=e.data.theme;}
    if(e.data.color){document.documentElement.dataset.pantokenColor=e.data.color;}
  }
});
p.postMessage({type:"pantoken-demo-request-theme"},"*");
```

**Collision point**: Each srcdoc iframe sets its own `<html data-pantoken-theme>` independently, but:
- All iframes query `postMessage` events from the same parent
- If two pantoken instances both broadcast, the last sender wins (or race condition)

### `/play` Runner

[tools/demo/runner/main.ts](tools/demo/runner/main.ts#L43-L80):
```ts
const HOST_ORIGIN = new URL(document.referrer || location.origin).origin;

function isDark(): boolean {
  try {
    if (window.parent && window.parent !== window) {
      return window.parent.document.documentElement.classList.contains("dark");
    }
  } catch {
    // Cross-origin parent
  }
  return matchMedia("(prefers-color-scheme: dark)").matches;
}

addEventListener("message", (e) => {
  if (e.data.type === "pantoken-demo-theme" && e.origin === HOST_ORIGIN) {
    // Apply theme from parent
  }
});
```

**Collision point**: Reads `window.parent.document.documentElement.classList` for dark mode. If the parent document belongs to two competing pantoken instances with different scheme states, the runner sees whichever one last modified `.dark` class.

---

## 5. Web Components: Prefix Scoping & foundationCss

### Register with Prefix

[renderers/web-components/src/lib/register-context.ts](renderers/web-components/src/lib/register-context.ts#L1-L100):
```ts
export const DEFAULT_PREFIX = "instui";

function resolvePrefix(prefix: string | null | undefined): string {
  return typeof prefix === "string" && prefix.trim() !== "" ? prefix : DEFAULT_PREFIX;
}

export function buildRegisterContext(
  options: RegisterContextOptions & { target?: ElementRegistry },
) {
  const prefix = resolvePrefix(options.prefix);
  const tag = (base: string) => `${prefix}-${base}`;
  // Every element definition rewritten: <instui-button> → <custom-prefix-button>
}
```

**Prefix rewriting**: Only affects **custom-element tag names** (`<instui-button>` vs `<custom-button>`), not CSS class names (always `.instui-button`).

### foundationCss Injection

**AGENTS.md notes** that `foundationCss()` is injected once into `document.head`, but **this is not actually done by web-components**. Instead:
- [formats/css/src/foundation.ts](formats/css/src/foundation.ts) emits elevation + focus-outline composites as a plugin
- Included in every ready-made sheet (`@pantoken/css`)
- Web-components assume the host document already has the token sheet loaded

**No per-instance injection**: Web-components rely on **inherited CSS custom properties** from the document; there's no per-instance foundationCss injection mechanism visible.

### Shadow DOM CSS Scoping

[renderers/web-components/src/lib/register-context.ts](renderers/web-components/src/lib/register-context.ts#L140-L170):
```ts
function makeWrapper(registry: ElementRegistry) {
  return (tag, css, render) => {
    registry.define(tag, class extends HTMLElement {
      paint(): void {
        if (this.shadowRoot) {
          this.shadowRoot.innerHTML = `<style>:host{display:inline-block}${css}</style>${render(this)}`;
        }
      }
    });
  };
}
```

**Collision point (minor)**: Each shadow root contains its own inlined component CSS (prefixed `.instui-`), but they all inherit `--instui-*` custom properties from **document.documentElement**. If two instances set conflicting `data-pantoken-theme` on the same root element, all shadow roots see the same tokens.

---

## 6. Instance, Scope, Namespace, Prefix Configuration

### Core / Tokens
[packages/core/src/build.ts](packages/core/src/build.ts#L33-L50): No instance/prefix config; emits canonical IR.

### CLI
[packages/cli/src/index.ts](packages/cli/src/index.ts#L40-L75):
```ts
noScope?: boolean;  // --no-scope flag for Pendo (removes @scope wrapper)
```
No instance namespace; tokens always named `--instui-*`.

### Plugin Kit
[packages/plugin-kit/src/index.ts](packages/plugin-kit): No prefix/namespace hooks exposed.

### Bundlers (Tailwind, Panda, PostCSS)
These typically accept a prefix option at the plugin level, but pantoken's built plugins don't expose instance-level configuration.

**Finding**: No built-in mechanism for namespace-prefixing custom properties (e.g., `--app1-color-brand` vs `--app2-color-brand`). All instances share `--instui-*` global namespace.

---

## 7. Concrete Collision Points

### A. Global localStorage Keys (Same-Origin Collision)

**File**: [docs/.vitepress/theme/theme.ts](docs/.vitepress/theme/theme.ts#L110-L120)  
**Lines**: 110–120  
**Problem**: Both instances write to `localStorage.getItem("pantoken-theme")` and `localStorage.getItem("pantoken-color")`

```ts
const STORAGE_KEY = "pantoken-theme";
const STORAGE_COLOR_KEY = "pantoken-color";

export function persistTheme(theme: PantokenTheme): void {
  localStorage.setItem(STORAGE_KEY, theme);  // ← Shared key
}
```

**Impact**: Last writer wins. If user toggles theme in one instance, the other reloads to the persisted value (from the first instance), causing desync.

---

### B. document.documentElement Attributes (Same-Document Collision)

**Files**:
- [docs/.vitepress/theme/theme.ts](docs/.vitepress/theme/theme.ts#L215-L230) (applyTheme, applyColor)

**Lines**: 215–230  
**Problem**: Both instances set `<html data-pantoken-theme>` and `<html data-pantoken-color>`

```ts
export function applyTheme(theme: PantokenTheme): void {
  const html = document.documentElement;
  html.dataset.pantokenTheme = theme;  // ← Single <html> element; last write wins
}
```

**Impact**: CSS scoped to `:root[data-pantoken-theme="canvas"]` sees whichever theme was last written. If Instance A sets `rebrand` and Instance B sets `canvas`, Instance A's theme selectors go inert, even though A is the active context.

---

### C. postMessage Broadcasting to Shared iframe Set (Same-Document Collision)

**File**: [docs/.vitepress/theme/theme.ts](docs/.vitepress/theme/theme.ts#L150-L180)  
**Lines**: 150–180  
**Problem**: Both instances query and broadcast to the same iframe set

```ts
export function broadcastTheme(theme: PantokenTheme, color: PantokenColor): void {
  for (const frame of document.querySelectorAll<HTMLIFrameElement>(
    ".pantoken-demo__frame, .canvas-rce-page__frame"  // ← Finds ALL on page
  )) {
    frame.contentWindow?.postMessage(
      { type: "pantoken-demo-theme", theme, color, mode: getActiveScheme() },
      themeTargetOrigin(frame)  // ← All frames get messaged
    );
  }
}
```

**Impact**: Both instances send conflicting postMessages to the same iframe. Depending on timing:
- Instance A sends `{ theme: "canvas", color: "navy" }`
- Instance B sends `{ theme: "rebrand", color: "blue" }`
- The iframe receives both; last one wins, and instance A's preview shows wrong theme

---

### D. CSS @property Global Registration (Browser-Global Collision)

**Files**:
- [formats/css/src/emit.ts](formats/css/src/emit.ts#L28-L35) (renderProperty)
- [docs/scripts/site-themes.ts](docs/scripts/site-themes.ts#L30-L45) (base theme with full @property registrations)

**Lines**: emit.ts 28–35; site-themes.ts 30–45  
**Problem**: `@property` declarations are **global to the entire document**. If two stylesheets both register `@property --instui-color-brand`, the second one overwrites the first

```ts
function renderProperty({ name, syntax, value }: PropertyRule): string {
  return [
    `@property ${name} {`,
    `  syntax: "${syntax}";`,
    `  inherits: ${inherits};`,
    `  initial-value: ${value.trim()};`,  // ← Global initial-value; no scoping
    `}`,
  ].join("\n");
}
```

**Impact**: Each sheet includes the full `@property` set. If Instance A loads rebrand tokens and Instance B loads canvas tokens (different concrete values), whichever loads last defines the `--instui-*` properties for the **entire document**. Variable shadow roots inherit the "winning" initial values.

---

### E. sheet Singleton Injection (No De-duplication Across Instances)

**File**: [formats/css/src/inject.ts](formats/css/src/inject.ts#L27-L40)  
**Lines**: 27–40  
**Problem**: `inject()` checks for `style[data-pantoken]`, but is only idempotent within a **single instance**. Two instances each calling `inject()` separately will each create their own `<style>` tag

```ts
export function inject(doc: Document | undefined = globalThis.document): HTMLStyleElement | undefined {
  const existing = doc.querySelector<HTMLStyleElement>("style[data-pantoken]");
  if (existing) return existing;  // ← Only one marker per instance

  const style = doc.createElement("style");
  style.setAttribute("data-pantoken", "css");
  style.textContent = css;
  doc.head.append(style);
  return style;
}
```

**Impact**: If Instance A and B both import `@pantoken/css/inject`, they each append their own `<style>` tag with potentially conflicting `@property` and `:root` declarations. The two sheets dueling for the same property names can cause unpredictable cascades.

---

### F. Parent/Child Window Access (Demo Runner Reading Host State)

**File**: [tools/demo/runner/main.ts](tools/demo/runner/main.ts#L60-L70)  
**Lines**: 60–70  
**Problem**: Demo runner reads **parent window's dark-mode state** directly; if two instances have conflicting `.dark` class, the runner misreads

```ts
function isDark(): boolean {
  try {
    if (window.parent && window.parent !== window) {
      return window.parent.document.documentElement.classList.contains("dark");  // ← Direct read of parent
    }
  } catch {
    // Cross-origin parent
  }
  return matchMedia("(prefers-color-scheme: dark)").matches;
}
```

**Impact**: If Instance A has `<html class="dark">` and Instance B removes it, runners embedded by both see inconsistent scheme state. Scheme is not broadscast; only read from parent on timer.

---

### G. Custom Theme Colors Attribute Scoping (Partial Mitigation, Still Collides on :root)

**Files**:
- [plugins/pantoken/custom-theme-colors/src/index.ts](plugins/pantoken/custom-theme-colors/src/index.ts#L1-L20)
- [plugins/pantoken/custom-theme-colors/README.md](plugins/pantoken/custom-theme-colors/README.md)

**Lines**: index.ts 1–20; README 16–22  
**Problem**: Two variants exist:
1. `:root[data-pantoken-color="navy"]` (both instances fight over :root attribute)
2. `[data-pantoken-color="navy"]` (scoped variant; can be placed on separate ancestors)

**Impact**: Using the scoped variant can isolate color schemes **within separate DOM subtrees** (e.g., docs chrome vs embedded preview wrapper), but both instances still collide on `:root[data-pantoken-theme="…"]` for theme selection, which is not element-scoped.

---

## Summary Table: Collision Mechanisms

| Collision Type | Scope | Severity | Affected Code | Mitigation |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| localStorage keys | Same-origin | High | theme.ts:110–120 | Namespace keys per instance (e.g., `app1-pantoken-theme`) |
| document.documentElement attributes | Single document | High | theme.ts:215–230 | Scope to a scoped element, not :root; use CSS :has() for cascade |
| postMessage broadcast targeting | Single page | High | theme.ts:150–180 | Query with instance-specific selector (e.g., `.app1-demo__frame`) |
| @property registrations | Global (browser) | **Critical** | emit.ts:28–35 | Prefix custom properties per instance (e.g., `--app1-instui-color-brand`); split into separate stylesheets |
| style[data-pantoken] singleton | Per-instance | Medium | inject.ts:27–40 | Use unique data-* markers per instance; de-duplicate at build time |
| parent window .dark class read | Cross-frame | Medium | runner/main.ts:60–70 | Broadcast scheme via postMessage; don't rely on DOM reads |
| theme CSS :root selectors | Global document | High | site-themes.ts:30–45 | Scope theme selectors to instance-specific ancestor (CSS :has() or @scope) |

---

## Recommended Isolation Patterns

1. **Per-instance prefix**: All custom properties → `--app<N>-color-brand` (requires forking @ build time)
2. **Element scoping**: Render each instance in a scoped ancestor; use `:root` only as last resort
3. **Unique iframe queries**: Query demo frames with instance-specific classes (`.app1-demo__frame` not `.pantoken-demo__frame`)
4. **Separate localStorage namespaces**: Prefix keys with instance identifier
5. **postMessage origin/target stricter filtering**: Ensure only the intended instance's broadcasts reach each iframe

## Multi-Pantoken Theme Scope Refactor — Implementation Details

---

### **1. formats/css: Full Source Listing & API Signatures**

**Directory structure:**
[src/](formats/css/src) contains:
- [to-css.ts](formats/css/src/to-css.ts) — main API
- [emit.ts](formats/css/src/emit.ts) — CSS builder
- [theme-variants.ts](formats/css/src/theme-variants.ts) — theme helpers
- [foundation.ts](formats/css/src/foundation.ts) — elevation/focus plugin
- [index.ts](formats/css/src/index.ts) — barrel
- [inject.ts](formats/css/src/inject.ts) — DOM side-effect entry

**Exported APIs** ([to-css.ts](formats/css/src/to-css.ts#L1-L65)):

```typescript
export interface ToCssOptions {
  scope?: string;  // selector for scoped declarations (default ":root")
  plugins?: readonly PantokenPlugin[];
}

export function toCss(tokens: readonly Token[], options: ToCssOptions = {}): string
  // Lines 65-100: extracts contextual (`var()` / `light-dark()`) tokens → declarations
  // concrete tokens → `@property` registrations; threads scope through buildCssFile()
```

**Scope threading** ([to-css.ts](formats/css/src/to-css.ts#L65-L100)):
```typescript
const { scope = ":root", plugins = [] } = options;  // L67
// Concrete vs contextual split (L70-74)
const properties: PropertyRule[] = [];  // @property rules (no light-dark)
const declarations: [string, string][] = [];  // :scope declarations
for (const token of tokens) {
  if (isContextual(token.value))  // /var\(|light-dark\(/
    declarations.push([token.name, token.value]);
  else
    properties.push({ name, syntax, value });
}
// Passed to buildCssFile with scope
let css = buildCssFile({
  scope,           // L82
  properties,
  sections: [{ pairs: declarations }],
});
```

**@property vs declarations split** ([emit.ts](formats/css/src/emit.ts#L50-L85)):
```typescript
export function buildCssFile({
  comments,
  scope,
  properties = [],
  sections,
  inherits = true,  // L64
}: {
  comments: string[];
  scope: string;    // selector for all sections (L65)
  properties?: PropertyRule[];  // global @property rules
  sections: CssSection[];       // L70-78: each section is [pairs] + optional layer
  inherits?: boolean;
}): string {
  const propertyBlock = properties.map((p) => renderProperty(p, inherits)).join("\n\n");
  // All properties emitted BEFORE sections (L75-76)
  const sectionBlocks = sections
    .filter((s) => s.pairs.length > 0)
    .map((s) => renderSection(scope, s));  // scope applied to each section's selector
  // ...returns [propertyBlock, ...sectionBlocks, ...].join("\n")
}
```

The split is **implicit in the IR**:
- Tokens with `light-dark()` or `var()` → cannot be `@property` initial-value (CSS rule) → routed to declarations
- Concrete hex/keyword tokens → can be `@property` initial-value → global `@property` block
- **No explicit "light-dark-only" split function exists yet** — it's checked at emit time via regex `isContextual()` ([to-css.ts L10-12](formats/css/src/to-css.ts#L10-12))

**light-dark() production** ([theme-variants.ts](formats/css/src/theme-variants.ts)):
- Tokens are already `light-dark()` wrapped in the IR (from `@pantoken/tokens` via `byTheme()`)
- Line 20-27: `lightBranch()` extracts light-mode value from `light-dark(light, dark)` for `lightOnly` mode
- No post-processing or lowering in this package — emitted as-is

**Published CSS files** ([package.json L18-27](formats/css/package.json#L18-27)):
```json
"exports": {
  "./style.css":                "./dist/style.css",
  "./style.lean.css":           "./dist/style.lean.css",
  "./style.rebrand.light.css":  "./dist/style.rebrand.light.css",
  "./style.rebrand.light.lean.css": "./dist/style.rebrand.light.lean.css",
  "./style.canvas.css":         "./dist/style.canvas.css",
  "./style.canvas.lean.css":    "./dist/style.canvas.lean.css",
  "./style.canvas-high-contrast.css": "./dist/style.canvas-high-contrast.css",
  "./style.canvas-high-contrast.lean.css": "./dist/style.canvas-high-contrast.lean.css"
}
```
Generated by `vp run generate` (script runs `pnpm generate` → [scripts/generate.ts](formats/css/scripts/generate.ts))

---

### **2. light-dark() Lowering: Build Config Analysis**

**No explicit light-dark() transform found** in workspace configs. Search results: empty. 

**Configs checked:**
- [vite.config.base.ts](vite.config.base.ts#L1-50) — workspace pack config, no browser target or lightningcss config
- [vite.config.ts](vite.config.ts#L1-70) — test + lint config only
- Root `vite.config.ts` has no `build.target` or postcss plugin that lowers `light-dark()`

**Current handling:**
- `light-dark()` **shipped as-is** to consumers in `.css` files
- Browsers supporting CSS spec's `light-dark()` render natively (Chrome 126+, Safari 17.4+)
